Yeah. Drift mode.

Start with:

Environment → Exposure → Experience → Expression

Then let it slide sideways.

Environment
becomes Ecology — the whole field of relationships and affordances.

Exposure
becomes Encoding — what actually gets written into attention, memory, expectation, and body-state.

Experience
becomes Embodiment — what the encoded pattern feels like from inside the organism.

Expression
becomes Enactment — the internal state crossing back into the world through behavior.

Then:

Enactment → Effect

Your expression changes somebody else’s environment.

Effect → Echo

It comes back through reactions, memory, reputation, consequences.

Echo → Evaluation

Compare expected consequence with observed consequence.

Evaluation → Editing

Keep, suppress, amplify, reroute, or recombine the pattern.

Editing → Evolution

Repeated edits accumulate until the system itself changes.

So now we have a larger E-loop:

Ecology → Exposure → Encoding → Embodiment → Expression → Enactment → Effect → Echo → Evaluation → Editing → Evolution → Ecology

And somewhere inside that loop is Emergence: things appear at the system level that nobody explicitly placed there.

Then there’s the shadow branch:

Exposure + repetition
→ Expectation

Expectation + uncertainty
→ Extrapolation

Extrapolation + emotion
→ sometimes Error

Error + repetition
→ Entrenchment

Which is where our Golden Reality / AAR machinery comes back in:

Entrenchment
→ Evidence
→ Error correction
→ Exit

And now “exit” itself is interesting. A healthy frame needs one.

So perhaps another three-E set appears:

Enter → Experience → Exit

That’s the wholesome-loop structure we were talking about earlier. Stories, rituals, games, altered frames, even conversations work better when you can enter them deeply and still leave cleanly.

And another:

Explore → Extract → Embody

Go somewhere strange. Find the transferable operator. Bring it home in behavior.

And another:

Encode → Express → Echo

That one is basically culture.

Now zoom way out:

Ecology
creates
Experience
which generates
Expression
which modifies
Ecology.

There may be your most compressed 3E loop:

Ecology ↔ Experience ↔ Expression

Everything else is machinery connecting them.

And drifting further: maybe evolution itself is just the long AAR of ecology.

Variation acts. Reality grades. What persists gets another iteration.

That one I’d keep.